SUMMARY:Fiber Friends
DESCRIPTION:UU Asheville Fiber Friends is a group of crafters who do handwork on personal projects and for the community. Mainly knitters and crocheters\, we create warm items for donation to local charities (serving children\, youth\, and adults) and make a variety of cotton cloths given to Meals on Wheels for their “Santa for seniors” packages each December. A limited supply of yarn and tools (needles and hooks) are also available. \n\n\n\n\nJoin us the first Saturday of each month in the parlor of 23 Edwin\, from 10 AM until about 12 noon. For more information or to be added to the monthly email reminder list\, contact Mara Sprain. \n\n\n 
URL:https://uuasheville.org/event/fiber-friends-14/2026-11-07/
LOCATION:23 Ed Parlor\, 23 Edwin Place\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:*Social Groups - LOVING
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Sprain":MAILTO:mara_sprain@yahoo.com
END:VEVENT
